@* ============================================================
   STEAM PHASE 1 — Original concept page
   Self-contained: all HTML, CSS, and JS live here.
   ============================================================ *@

<div class="se-page">

    <!-- NAV removed — handled by shell tab bar -->
    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="se-hero">
        <div class="se-hero-grid"></div>

        <span class="se-badge">CONCEPT DESIGN · OPEN SOURCE IDEA</span>

        <h1>
            The <span>Steam-Electric</span><br />
            Vehicle System
        </h1>

        <p>
            A closed-loop steam propulsion concept using battery-powered heating,
            PWM control, and multi-axle electric motors.
            Built around existing technology and thermodynamic principles.
        </p>

        <div class="se-hero-stats">
            <div class="se-stat"><div class="n">3×</div><div class="l">Concept torque advantage</div></div>
            <div class="se-stat"><div class="n">0</div><div class="l">Combustion events</div></div>
            <div class="se-stat"><div class="n">~40</div><div class="l">Illustrative moving parts</div></div>
            <div class="se-stat"><div class="n">H₂O</div><div class="l">Working fluid</div></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CONCEPT -->
    <div id="concept">
        <section class="se-section">
            <div class="se-section-sub">The Idea</div>
            <h2 class="se-section-title">Three component swaps. One electrical overhaul.</h2>
            <p class="se-section-lead">
                This concept explores replacing the conventional combustion powertrain
                with a steam-based mechanical system and electrical architecture.
                The chassis, suspension, brakes, and body could remain conceptually
                separate from the propulsion system.
            </p>

            <div class="se-card-grid">
                <div class="se-card">
                    <div class="se-card-icon">🔁</div>
                    <h3>Engine → Steam Cylinders</h3>
                    <p>A steam piston engine can provide mechanical torque through a crankshaft. A double-acting multi-cylinder configuration is shown here as a conceptual architecture.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="se-card">
                    <div class="se-card-icon">💧</div>
                    <h3>Fuel Tank → Water Tank</h3>
                    <p>Water acts as the working fluid. A condenser can recover exhaust steam and return condensed water to the system.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="se-card">
                    <div class="se-card-icon">⚡</div>
                    <h3>Generator Loop</h3>
                    <p>The steam engine can mechanically drive a generator while electric motors provide propulsion in an electric-drive architecture.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="se-card">
                    <div class="se-card-icon">🎛</div>
                    <h3>PWM Controller = Heat Control</h3>
                    <p>A power controller can regulate electrical heating input. Actual thermal efficiency depends on the heater, boiler, insulation, operating pressure, and cycle design.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="se-card">
                    <div class="se-card-icon">🔄</div>
                    <h3>Closed Loop by Design</h3>
                    <p>Water can be evaporated, expanded, condensed, and returned to the feed system. Some makeup water may still be required.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="se-card">
                    <div class="se-card-icon">🏭</div>
                    <h3>Manufacturing Concept</h3>
                    <p>The design attempts to reduce some conventional combustion components, while recognizing that boilers, pumps, condensers, controls, and pressure hardware introduce their own complexity.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>

    <!-- SCHEMATIC -->
    <div class="se-section-full" id="schematic">
        <section class="se-section">
            <div class="se-section-sub">System Architecture</div>
            <h2 class="se-section-title">Closed-loop schematic</h2>
            <p class="se-section-lead">
                Battery power supplies electrical heating. Steam expands through the mechanical power unit,
                which can drive a generator. A condenser recovers the working fluid.
            </p>

            <div class="se-schematic">
                <svg width="100%" viewBox="0 0 680 520" role="img" aria-label="Steam-electric closed loop schematic">
                    <title>Steam-electric closed loop schematic</title>
                    <defs>
                        <marker id="p1sarr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                            <path d="M2 1L8 5L2 9" fill="none" stroke="context-stroke" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
                        </marker>
                    </defs>

                    <!-- Battery -->
                    <rect x="20" y="30" width="130" height="56" rx="8" fill="#0a2040" stroke="#4ab4ff" stroke-width="1" />
                    <text x="85" y="54" text-anchor="middle" fill="#4ab4ff" font-size="13" font-weight="600">Battery Pack</text>
                    <text x="85" y="72" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5a8aaa" font-size="11">Battery / capacitor</text>

                    <!-- Heating Element -->
                    <rect x="20" y="140" width="130" height="56" rx="8" fill="#1a0f00" stroke="#ff7a30" stroke-width="1" />
                    <text x="85" y="164" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ff9a50" font-size="13" font-weight="600">Heating Element</text>
                    <text x="85" y="182" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8a5a30" font-size="11">PWM controlled</text>

                    <!-- Battery → Heater -->
                    <line x1="85" y1="86" x2="85" y2="138" stroke="#4ab4ff" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#p1sarr)" class="p1-pulse-anim" />
                    <text x="100" y="116" fill="#4ab4ff" font-size="11">DC power</text>

                    <!-- Water Tank -->
                    <rect x="20" y="250" width="130" height="56" rx="8" fill="#001a30" stroke="#30a0ff" stroke-width="1" />
                    <text x="85" y="274" text-anchor="middle" fill="#30a0ff" font-size="13" font-weight="600">Water Tank</text>
                    <text x="85" y="292" text-anchor="middle" fill="#3a6a8a" font-size="11">Feedwater system</text>

                    <!-- Heater → Water -->
                    <line x1="85" y1="196" x2="85" y2="248" stroke="#ff7a30" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none" marker-end="url(#p1sarr)" />
                    <text x="100" y="226" fill="#ff7a30" font-size="11">heat</text>

                    <!-- Steam Output -->
                    <rect x="20" y="360" width="130" height="56" rx="8" fill="#1a1200" stroke="#ffaa00" stroke-width="1" />
                    <text x="85" y="384" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffcc44" font-size="13" font-weight="600">Steam Output</text>
                    <text x="85" y="402" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8a7a30" font-size="11">High pressure</text>

                    <!-- Water → Steam -->
